@vaxerski the gtk issue looks to me like it is related to `_GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS`.
On x11 gtk checks if the window manager supports it, and if it reports support, gtk will draw shadows, possibly rounded corners and some other stuff. The window will get the `_GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS` atom that contains the real size the window should have, so you have to position the window accordingly.

I am not certain how this is handled on wayland, but you might want to look into this, otherwise you will have a lot of issues with GTK in the future.

This diff appears to fix the for me:

```patch
diff --git a/src/helpers/MiscFunctions.cpp b/src/helpers/MiscFunctions.cpp
index bf8724c..61ae0c4 100644
--- a/src/helpers/MiscFunctions.cpp
+++ b/src/helpers/MiscFunctions.cpp
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ std::string removeBeginEndSpacesTabs(std::string str) {
         str = str.substr(1);
     }
 
-    while (str[str.length() - 1] == ' ' || str[str.length() - 1] == '\t') {
+    while (str.length() != 0 && (str[str.length() - 1] == ' ' || str[str.length() - 1] == '\t')) {
         str = str.substr(0, str.length() - 1);
     }
 
```

Let me know if I should open a PR for this or if there's something I'm missing here.

